<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the Therr iOS app.

  KEEP IN SYNC WITH THREE OTHER PLACES. All four must agree, or App Review and
  regulators will find the discrepancy before you do:
    1. This file
    2. The App Store Connect "App Privacy" nutrition label (edited by hand in
       App Store Connect - updating this file does NOT update the label)
    3. The Google Play Data Safety form
    4. The published Privacy Policy at https://www.therr.app/privacy-policy.html

  NSPrivacyTracking is false: the app does not link user data with third-party
  data for advertising or measurement, and does not share it with data brokers.
  It therefore presents no App Tracking Transparency prompt. If that ever
  changes, this flag, NSPrivacyTrackingDomains, the ATT prompt, and the Privacy
  Policy's no-sale/no-share statements all have to change together.

  Third-party SDKs (Firebase, Google Analytics, Stripe, Google Maps) ship their
  own signed privacy manifests; this file covers first-party collection only.
-->
